# PostgreSQL 16 — `postgresql.conf` (Ubuntu)

Canonical settings from **`/etc/postgresql/16/main/postgresql.conf`** on the Ubuntu app/DB host (`192.168.222.202` / xbox2).

**Data directory:** `/var/lib/postgresql/16/main` (not `/mnt/pgdata16` — that mount is app media).  
**Port:** `50010`. Reload/restart after edits: `sudo systemctl reload postgresql@16-main` (or restart if `port` / `data_directory` / `listen_addresses` change).

```conf
data_directory = '/var/lib/postgresql/16/main'          # use data in another directory
hba_file = '/etc/postgresql/16/main/pg_hba.conf'        # host-based authentication file
ident_file = '/etc/postgresql/16/main/pg_ident.conf'    # ident configuration file
external_pid_file = '/var/run/postgresql/16-main.pid'                   # write an extra PID file
#port = 5432                            # (change requires restart)
port = 50010                            # (change requires restart)
max_connections = 100                   # (change requires restart)
unix_socket_directories = '/var/run/postgresql' # comma-separated list of directories
ssl = on
ssl_cert_file = '/etc/ssl/certs/ssl-cert-snakeoil.pem'
ssl_key_file = '/etc/ssl/private/ssl-cert-snakeoil.key'
shared_buffers = 128MB                  # min 128kB
dynamic_shared_memory_type = posix      # the default is usually the first option
max_wal_size = 1GB
min_wal_size = 80MB
log_line_prefix = '%m [%p] %q%u@%d '            # special values:
log_timezone = 'America/New_York'
cluster_name = '16/main'                        # added to process titles if nonempty
datestyle = 'iso, mdy'
timezone = 'America/New_York'
lc_messages = 'en_US.UTF-8'             # locale for system error message
lc_monetary = 'en_US.UTF-8'             # locale for monetary formatting
lc_numeric = 'en_US.UTF-8'              # locale for number formatting
lc_time = 'en_US.UTF-8'                 # locale for time formatting
default_text_search_config = 'pg_catalog.english'
include_dir = 'conf.d'                  # include files ending in '.conf' from

#andrewton 03/31/2026
search_path = 'helloworldjunktest, public'

#below is need for MAC to DBeaver to ubuntu DB
listen_addresses = '*'

##### AndrewTon, 6/2026, auto cleanup/optimize indexes
# Make autovacuum wake up more frequently to check for work (Default is 1min)
autovacuum_naptime = 15s

# Trigger a vacuum when 10% of a table's rows are dead (Default is 20%)
autovacuum_vacuum_scale_factor = 0.10

# Trigger an analyze when 5% of rows change (Default is 10%)
autovacuum_analyze_scale_factor = 0.05

# Give autovacuum more memory to work faster (Default is usually low)
autovacuum_work_mem = 256MB
```
